<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">13052026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Israel has quietly authorised thirty-four new West Bank settlements... its largest single batch on record, approved in late March while the world's attention was fixed on the Iran war.</s> <s>The vote unlocks permanent water and electricity hookups, entrenching each outpost in occupied Palestine and stripping land tenure from communities nearby.</s> <s>The displacement the news cycle stopped noticing hasn't stopped — it's accelerated under cover of a larger war.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>BRICS foreign ministers met in Delhi this week and failed to agree a joint statement on Iran.</s> <s>Russia and China back Tehran, the Emirates opposes it, and India has declared neutrality, leaving the bloc with no common position ahead of its September summit.</s> <s>Western capitals read the silence as paralysis, but BRICS was built as a consensus of the non-aligned, not a counter-alliance — so the ceiling on Iran's diplomatic support is itself the news.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India's prime minister has halved his own motorcade as part of an austerity push tied to rising crude prices.</s> <s>Narendra Modi cited the Iran war's fuel bill, and ruling-party chief ministers in the states followed within days, while an electric vehicle plan for official convoys is now circulating.</s> <s>It's a small, performative gesture, but it shows how a war four thousand kilometres from Delhi is reshaping domestic political theatre.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kuwait has arrested four members of Iran's Revolutionary Guards on Bubiyan Island, a low-lying outpost that controls Khor Abdullah — Iraq's only sea access to the Gulf.</s> <s>The arrests happened on the first of May, and Tehran hasn't acknowledged them publicly.</s> <s>It opens a quiet new maritime front in a war that until now had stayed mostly above the waterline.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Five years into the junta's rule, no independent outlet operates legally inside Myanmar.</s> <s>Exiled reporters file daily from Mae Sot, Kuala Lumpur and Delhi, and the Committee to Protect Journalists ranks Myanmar among the world's leading jailers of the press.</s> <s>This is what a captured media landscape looks like at year five, and global press indifference is now part of the architecture.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's fiscal deficit has collapsed to zero point seven percent of <sub alias="gross domestic product">GDP</sub>, the lowest level in nearly three decades.</s> <s>The Finance Ministry credits a forty-five percent surge in the petroleum levy, which has become the government's single largest revenue source as defence and subsidy spending kept rising.</s> <s>That headline turnaround is real — but it was paid for by motorists, not the budget hawks who'll be credited for it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A one point five billion dollar Trump Tower project on Australia's Gold Coast has collapsed after just three months.</s> <s>Developer Altus called the Trump brand toxic to Australians in the climate around the Iran war, while the Trump Organization blamed unpaid obligations.</s> <s>It's a small but clean datum on a larger phenomenon... presidential brand value as a financing input has turned negative in allied markets.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A torpedo sank the Russian-flagged Ursa Major off the coast of Spain before its cargo of submarine propulsion reactors could reach North Korea, Spanish investigators now say.</s> <s>UN sanctions explicitly bar such nuclear transfers to Pyongyang, and Madrid is treating the sinking as a sanctions-enforcement matter rather than an act of war.</s> <s>Who fired the torpedo hasn't been disclosed, and that absence is itself a diplomatic choice.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>American energy prices rose seventeen point nine percent in April, dragging the Consumer Price Index to three point eight percent — a three-year high.</s> <s>The Bureau of Labor Statistics attributes the spike to Iran's closure of the Strait of Hormuz, through which a fifth of global oil flows.</s> <s>Rate cuts this year are off the table now, and Federal Reserve officials are openly discussing hikes — a war's energy passthrough rewriting the policy outlook of the world's largest economy.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Chile's new government has moved to gut a globally unusual instrument that placed thirty-one stretches of coastline under Indigenous management.</s> <s>The Lafkenche Act of two thousand eight gave Mapuche and Williche communities legal authority over near-shore marine zones — the only such model in Latin America — and weeks into office, President Kast's administration announced amendments to open those waters to industrial development.</s> <s>What's at stake is whether Indigenous coastal governance survives as a precedent anywhere on the continent.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Colombia has lost eight hundred thousand hectares of Amazon rainforest in the decade since its peace accord with the <sub alias="F A R C">FARC</sub>.</s> <s>Land tenure was left unresolved in the agreement, and splinter groups have occupied vacated territories, converting them to coca fields and cattle pasture.</s> <s>President Petro's Total Peace Programme now offers agroforestry and tourism as alternatives, but the forest doesn't grow back on a political timetable.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>One hundred and fifty million hectares have already burned globally this year, with Africa's fire record broken by twenty-three percent through April and Asia's by forty.</s> <s>World Weather Attribution warns that an El Niño forming this month, layered onto climate change, risks unprecedented weather extremes later in the year.</s> <s>The fire year is barely a third gone, and the curve is steeper than any modelled scenario predicted.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Zambia has postponed RightsCon — the largest in-person digital-rights gathering in the world — just three weeks before three thousand seven hundred delegates were due to arrive in Lusaka.</s> <s>Beijing pressured Lusaka to exclude Taiwan from the conference, organisers refused, and the postponement followed.</s> <s>Digital-rights group <sub alias="S M E X">SMEX</sub> warns this gives any future host government a template — civil-society infrastructure isn't as venue-portable as it looked.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Taiwan's advanced semiconductor fabs sit one hundred and eighty kilometres from mainland China.</s> <s>The island controls the world's most sophisticated chip supply, and Chinese and American negotiators are meeting in Beijing this week, with access to Taiwan's foundries reportedly on the table.</s> <s>Any escalation around the strait would be an instant supply shock for every server, phone and weapons system downstream — and that's most of them.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Britain has vetoed a two billion dollar Scottish wind turbine factory proposed by China's Mingyang on national security grounds.</s> <s>Denmark's Vestas announced a rival factory at the same Scottish port the very same day.</s> <s>BloombergNEF warns that fewer supply routes raise European project costs, and Europe is now discovering the price of tech sovereignty inside its own net-zero timeline.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>